WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:04.704
WINSTON CHANG: All right.

00:00:04.704 --> 00:00:08.241
Well, today we're going
to talk about making

00:00:08.241 --> 00:00:12.245
a Wordle app or an app
like Wordle, I should say.

00:00:12.245 --> 00:00:16.282
Basically, you type in a
word that's five letters

00:00:16.282 --> 00:00:22.355
and then you hit Enter,
you click a button

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:25.625
and then it checks how many
of the letters in that word

00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:28.461
are correct or are present
in the target word,

00:00:28.461 --> 00:00:30.263
and then it prints
that out and then you

00:00:30.263 --> 00:00:32.399
hit Enter in another word,
and you just keep going.

00:00:32.399 --> 00:00:34.234
So that's a pretty simple--

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:36.036
that's a pretty simple thing.

00:00:36.436 --> 00:00:39.439
So for our
Wordle app, our overall strategy is going to be to

00:00:39.472 --> 00:00:42.976
first work on the
logic of the application and get that all working.

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:47.747
And then once that's
done, we will make it look pretty using some CSS

00:00:47.747 --> 00:00:51.718
and a little bit of JavaScript,
and we'll do that in a later video in this series.

00:00:51.751 --> 00:00:55.455
What you're seeing
here is the actual Shiny Wordle app at the end.

00:00:55.989 --> 00:00:59.893
And this does take a little
bit of CSS and JavaScript work, but it can be done.

00:01:00.126 --> 00:01:05.465
So you know the way that I look
to get started with problems

00:01:05.465 --> 00:01:09.436
like these is to just start with
something really, really basic

00:01:09.436 --> 00:01:10.937
and then build it up.

00:01:10.937 --> 00:01:14.174
So there's some problems
where that's not really

00:01:14.174 --> 00:01:19.446
the appropriate approach,
but for something like this,

00:01:19.446 --> 00:01:20.680
I think that's the way to go.

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:23.583
So first, we'll
work on the logic,

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:25.819
and then later on, we can
work on making it look nice.

00:01:25.819 --> 00:01:29.322
But the first thing
is to get the game

00:01:29.322 --> 00:01:31.057
logic working properly.

00:01:31.057 --> 00:01:31.558
All right.

00:01:31.558 --> 00:01:34.961
So we've got our studio started.

00:01:34.961 --> 00:01:38.498
And I also already
have my word list here.

00:01:38.498 --> 00:01:41.167
So I won't go into the
depth about how to do that,

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:43.670
but it's there.

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:46.906
So let's start with by
making a simple Shiny app.

00:01:46.906 --> 00:01:51.511
Library Shiny, the UI is--

00:01:51.511 --> 00:01:55.415
let's start with a fluidPage.

00:01:55.415 --> 00:01:58.651
And I'm just going to put
in a textInput for now.

00:01:58.651 --> 00:01:59.152
All right.

00:01:59.152 --> 00:02:01.287
So that's the thing
that-- how people interact

00:02:01.287 --> 00:02:03.790
with it is they type in
text [? into ?] input,

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:07.327
textInput, call it, guess.

00:02:07.327 --> 00:02:10.897
And actually, we won't
put a label on it.

00:02:10.897 --> 00:02:13.133
And all right.

00:02:13.133 --> 00:02:13.666
There's that.

00:02:13.666 --> 00:02:22.275
And server function(input,
output.) And actually-- sorry.

00:02:22.275 --> 00:02:24.844
The first thing I'll do is not
just have people typing input,

00:02:24.844 --> 00:02:26.846
but I'll just have it
print out what they typed.

00:02:26.846 --> 00:02:32.185
So we'll do a
verbatim text output.

00:02:32.185 --> 00:02:35.622
Let's load up Shiny so we
can just auto-complete.

00:02:35.622 --> 00:02:40.693
Great, textOutput,
call it, results.

00:02:40.693 --> 00:02:42.862
Oh, and also, a little tip.

00:02:42.862 --> 00:02:46.466
Would be placeholder
equals true.

00:02:46.466 --> 00:02:46.966
OK.

00:02:46.966 --> 00:02:49.435
So then that will just
make it so textOutput

00:02:49.435 --> 00:02:50.336
is always visible.

00:02:50.336 --> 00:02:52.372
Otherwise, when there's
no content in it,

00:02:52.372 --> 00:02:53.606
it's not visible.

00:02:53.606 --> 00:02:56.442
So it can be a
little bit surprising

00:02:56.442 --> 00:02:59.679
if it sort of appears
out of nowhere

00:02:59.679 --> 00:03:03.049
or disappears when
there's no content there.

00:03:03.049 --> 00:03:03.550
OK.

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:09.656
So let's see it's your output
results and for right now

00:03:09.656 --> 00:03:12.292
we're just going to have it echo
the text that these were types

00:03:12.292 --> 00:03:13.660
in.

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:14.160
The text.

00:03:18.031 --> 00:03:25.138
We'll do input$guess.

00:03:25.138 --> 00:03:27.373
And then ShinyApp(ui, server).

00:03:29.909 --> 00:03:30.410
OK.

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:34.013
So now RStudio
recognizes it's an app

00:03:34.013 --> 00:03:36.082
and just for
convenience, this is

00:03:36.082 --> 00:03:38.618
a little thing I wanted to show
up in the little Viewer panel

00:03:38.618 --> 00:03:40.153
down here.

00:03:40.153 --> 00:03:44.524
So I already have it set up that
way, and I'll click run app,

00:03:44.524 --> 00:03:45.525
and here's my app.

00:03:45.525 --> 00:03:47.160
Hello.

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:48.595
It shows Hello, there.

00:03:48.595 --> 00:03:49.095
All right.

00:03:49.095 --> 00:03:53.600
So that's the very
start of our Wordle app.

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:55.868
So right now, it's
a little bit--

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:58.371
every time I type anything,
it's going to show it down here.

00:03:58.371 --> 00:04:02.675
But I only really wanted to
do something with the input

00:04:02.675 --> 00:04:04.043
when I say I'm ready.

00:04:04.043 --> 00:04:07.914
So I'm going to-- and I'm going
to do that by adding a button.

00:04:07.914 --> 00:04:13.353
So I say actionButton,
and we'll call it Go.

00:04:13.353 --> 00:04:16.923
And we'll label it Go.

00:04:16.923 --> 00:04:21.261
And now we have this
renderText here.

00:04:21.261 --> 00:04:23.630
There's actually a number
of ways we can do this,

00:04:23.630 --> 00:04:28.868
but I'll show you one of
like the sort of relatively

00:04:28.868 --> 00:04:29.736
new ways of doing it.

00:04:29.736 --> 00:04:31.271
I can add it, I
can use bindEvent.

00:04:31.271 --> 00:04:38.077
So if you're familiar with like
eventReactive or observeEvent,

00:04:38.077 --> 00:04:43.316
you can have those things
run only when a particular--

00:04:43.316 --> 00:04:45.551
when some other
reactive thing happens.

00:04:45.551 --> 00:04:47.553
So like when a
button is clicked.

00:04:47.553 --> 00:04:48.921
And so you can
actually bindEvent

00:04:48.921 --> 00:04:51.991
with reactives and observers,
but you can also use it

00:04:51.991 --> 00:04:53.159
with these vender functions.

00:04:53.159 --> 00:04:57.030
So I can say
bindEvent(input$go).

00:04:57.030 --> 00:04:57.530
OK.

00:04:57.530 --> 00:05:05.171
So it will only update
this or execute this

00:05:05.171 --> 00:05:09.475
and update the result text
when the Go button is pressed.

00:05:09.475 --> 00:05:11.311
And I still haven't
figured out the best way

00:05:11.311 --> 00:05:12.545
to do indentation for this.

00:05:12.545 --> 00:05:14.080
It looks a little funny here.

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:16.549
And I'm using the
new R 4.1 style

00:05:16.549 --> 00:05:20.620
pipe here since I'm running that
version of R. And I'll save it

00:05:20.620 --> 00:05:21.754
and reload.

00:05:21.754 --> 00:05:28.127
So I say, hello and nothing
should happen until I press Go.

00:05:28.127 --> 00:05:31.397
Say goodbye, and get nothing
happens until I press Go.

00:05:31.397 --> 00:05:34.233
And now-- and it's just
replacing the content

00:05:34.233 --> 00:05:38.871
of this text output right now.

00:05:38.871 --> 00:05:44.577
So now's a good time to start
doing something well with that.

00:05:44.577 --> 00:05:46.846
OK, so let's see.

00:05:46.846 --> 00:05:47.980
One thing that-- let's see.

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:48.915
How do we do this?

00:05:48.915 --> 00:05:52.552
So in Wordle, all
of your guesses

00:05:52.552 --> 00:05:58.024
are limited to words
that are five characters.

00:05:58.024 --> 00:06:00.093
And actually on top of
that, they're actually

00:06:00.093 --> 00:06:02.862
limited to words that are
in a particular word list,

00:06:02.862 --> 00:06:08.968
but let's just start off by
limiting it to five characters

00:06:08.968 --> 00:06:13.473
first, and then we'll make use
of the word list after that.

00:06:13.473 --> 00:06:14.307
So let's see.

00:06:14.307 --> 00:06:19.379
So we can take
input$guess and let's say,

00:06:19.379 --> 00:06:29.722
if nchar(input$guess) is
not equal to five then--

00:06:29.722 --> 00:06:35.061
well, I'll show the naive
way of doing it first

00:06:35.061 --> 00:06:37.597
and then do something a
little bit more sophisticated.

00:06:37.597 --> 00:06:40.133
And then-- so if it's
not five characters,

00:06:40.133 --> 00:06:42.635
then we'll just return out
of this random text function

00:06:42.635 --> 00:06:44.537
[INAUDIBLE] nothing
or actually maybe we

00:06:44.537 --> 00:06:46.873
should return an empty string.

00:06:46.873 --> 00:06:50.710
And if it is five
characters, then we move on

00:06:50.710 --> 00:06:57.917
and I'll have it show this text.

00:06:57.917 --> 00:07:00.253
So paste.

00:07:00.253 --> 00:07:04.924
You entered input$guess.

00:07:07.960 --> 00:07:10.363
All right, reload.

00:07:10.363 --> 00:07:16.736
So I can say abc and if I click
on here, nothing should happen.

00:07:16.736 --> 00:07:20.173
But if I say hello--
which is five characters,

00:07:20.173 --> 00:07:22.809
they'll say you entered hello.

00:07:22.809 --> 00:07:28.414
And if I say goodbye, which
is seven characters long,

00:07:28.414 --> 00:07:31.217
well, it's not printing
out, "you entered goodbye,"

00:07:31.217 --> 00:07:34.120
but it is just making
the result disappear.

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:36.956
So that's actually not
really what we want either.

00:07:36.956 --> 00:07:40.560
And there is a function
in Shiny called

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:43.930
req like for short for require.

00:07:43.930 --> 00:07:46.766
I mean, you can use
it to exit out of here

00:07:46.766 --> 00:07:55.741
and not replace the previous
contents of this output.

00:07:55.741 --> 00:07:57.043
So we can say, req(FALSE).

00:08:01.614 --> 00:08:02.114
OK.

00:08:02.114 --> 00:08:05.585
Actually normally if we just do
req.req(FALSE) and we do this.

00:08:05.585 --> 00:08:12.091
So if I say hello,
goodbye, it will still

00:08:12.091 --> 00:08:13.526
like-- it'll still clear this.

00:08:13.526 --> 00:08:17.763
But what we need to say
is req(FALSE) cancelOutput

00:08:17.763 --> 00:08:20.333
equals TRUE.

00:08:20.333 --> 00:08:28.641
So cancelOutput means when
you hit this line of code,

00:08:28.641 --> 00:08:31.611
don't modify any downstream
outputs that are from this.

00:08:31.611 --> 00:08:33.412
And this actually
isn't an output itself.

00:08:33.412 --> 00:08:35.581
But if these were like in
a reactive expression that

00:08:35.581 --> 00:08:40.620
was consumed by an
output then that output

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:41.687
would also not change.

00:08:41.687 --> 00:08:45.157
So I'll say, hello
again and goodbye.

00:08:45.157 --> 00:08:47.660
And when I click
on this, now it's

00:08:47.660 --> 00:08:51.664
not erasing the previous
contents of this render text.

00:08:51.664 --> 00:08:52.999
Oh, great.

00:08:52.999 --> 00:08:54.834
And now we can compare it to--

00:08:54.834 --> 00:08:56.469
I guess we can compare
it to word list.

00:08:56.469 --> 00:09:02.441
So at the top of this app,
let's say source(wordlist), OK.

00:09:02.441 --> 00:09:07.847
And in this word, this is
actually two sets of words--

00:09:07.847 --> 00:09:11.117
there's common words which are--

00:09:11.117 --> 00:09:14.220
that's a list of like
2,500 words which

00:09:14.220 --> 00:09:15.488
are relatively common.

00:09:15.488 --> 00:09:19.692
Are the most common
2,500 words in English.

00:09:19.692 --> 00:09:22.094
And then there's a
larger list of words that

00:09:22.094 --> 00:09:25.398
are like all five-letter words.

00:09:25.398 --> 00:09:30.770
The shorter list is ones that
are, I guess, the target words.

00:09:30.770 --> 00:09:33.873
And the longer list
R is a set of words

00:09:33.873 --> 00:09:36.242
that users can use to guess.

00:09:36.242 --> 00:09:37.710
But some of them
are really obscure

00:09:37.710 --> 00:09:39.946
and it would be
really, really hard

00:09:39.946 --> 00:09:41.681
if those were the target words.

00:09:41.681 --> 00:09:44.884
So oops, let's
source(wordlist.R).

00:09:44.884 --> 00:09:46.819
And let's see.

00:09:46.819 --> 00:09:48.554
Actually, let's
just run that, oops.

00:09:48.554 --> 00:09:50.656
Good Let's put that there.

00:09:50.656 --> 00:09:51.657
source(wordlist.R).

00:09:51.657 --> 00:09:55.161
OK, we have words
common_5 and words all_5.

00:09:55.161 --> 00:09:58.197
So those are the two
character vectors

00:09:58.197 --> 00:09:59.932
we have that have--
contain all the words.

00:10:02.635 --> 00:10:08.908
So right now, we just want to--

00:10:08.908 --> 00:10:10.376
right now, we just
want to show--

00:10:13.479 --> 00:10:16.916
right now, we just want
to move on from here

00:10:16.916 --> 00:10:20.119
if the word that they
entered is an actual word

00:10:20.119 --> 00:10:22.688
in the words_all list.

00:10:22.688 --> 00:10:33.165
So we can say, if input$guess
is in words_all, I've actually--

00:10:33.165 --> 00:10:35.434
sorry.

00:10:35.434 --> 00:10:37.269
So we have processed there.

00:10:37.269 --> 00:10:43.609
If it's not in or it's
all_5 then cancel output.

00:10:43.609 --> 00:10:44.110
OK.

00:10:44.110 --> 00:10:45.578
So let's run it.

00:10:45.578 --> 00:10:48.648
And again, hello
should work but we

00:10:48.648 --> 00:10:51.884
just type in some
random five characters,

00:10:51.884 --> 00:10:53.986
that should have no effect.

00:10:53.986 --> 00:10:54.487
OK.

00:10:54.487 --> 00:10:57.890
So that's pretty good.

00:10:57.890 --> 00:11:00.626
Now, we can actually start--

00:11:00.626 --> 00:11:06.632
we can use a target word and
start processing people's

00:11:06.632 --> 00:11:09.468
guesses for that target word.

00:11:09.468 --> 00:11:10.269
Let's see.

00:11:10.269 --> 00:11:14.240
So we can do it.

00:11:14.240 --> 00:11:17.143
Well, we can do it inside
the server function.

00:11:17.143 --> 00:11:19.378
If we select a random word
inside the server function,

00:11:19.378 --> 00:11:22.114
that means that each time
somebody connects to this,

00:11:22.114 --> 00:11:24.483
they'll get a different word.

00:11:24.483 --> 00:11:29.221
And if we select a random word
outside of the server function,

00:11:29.221 --> 00:11:35.861
then it will-- as long as
this app is running and you

00:11:35.861 --> 00:11:38.564
don't restart or quit
the app or something--

00:11:38.564 --> 00:11:40.666
I mean, close the
app from the R side,

00:11:40.666 --> 00:11:44.904
then everyone will
get the same word.

00:11:44.904 --> 00:11:46.205
I mean, let's do it that way.

00:11:46.205 --> 00:11:48.074
So there's words_common_5.

00:11:48.074 --> 00:11:57.116
So we can just say target
is sample words_common_5, 1.

00:11:57.116 --> 00:12:00.986
I think that's the
right sample for--

00:12:04.924 --> 00:12:05.424
Yep.

00:12:05.424 --> 00:12:06.592
Just sample one of them.

00:12:06.592 --> 00:12:08.294
So and actually, of
course, we can always

00:12:08.294 --> 00:12:09.628
just run this at the counsel.

00:12:09.628 --> 00:12:11.130
We've got stop the app first.

00:12:14.100 --> 00:12:14.600
Yeah.

00:12:14.600 --> 00:12:16.102
So that picks out
one word-- duchy.

00:12:16.102 --> 00:12:17.236
That would be really hard.

00:12:20.172 --> 00:12:23.109
Yet another thing you
could do is do like a--

00:12:23.109 --> 00:12:25.010
set of random seed
based on the date.

00:12:27.480 --> 00:12:28.047
I don't know.

00:12:28.047 --> 00:12:32.618
You probably do like as integer.

00:12:32.618 --> 00:12:33.486
You know, Sys.Date.

00:12:38.124 --> 00:12:39.158
OK, so yeah.

00:12:39.158 --> 00:12:43.162
So let's try this.

00:12:43.162 --> 00:12:45.898
And then oops.

00:12:45.898 --> 00:12:47.066
I guess we can print it out.

00:12:47.066 --> 00:12:49.969
So for today, the
target word is gives.

00:12:49.969 --> 00:12:51.971
And then if we run
this all again--

00:12:51.971 --> 00:12:58.377
so let's say the app shuts down
or if you're running this on--

00:12:58.377 --> 00:13:00.946
if you're running this on a
