00:13:06.752 --> 00:13:11.190
So let's run this again and
again if we would run target.

00:13:11.190 --> 00:13:13.793
It's still gives.

00:13:13.793 --> 00:13:16.762
So anybody who connects
today would have that word.

00:13:16.762 --> 00:13:20.599
And I guess that actually works.

00:13:20.599 --> 00:13:21.834
Let's use that method for now.

00:13:21.834 --> 00:13:24.370
OK, so yeah.

00:13:24.370 --> 00:13:26.839
So today the target
word is gives

00:13:26.839 --> 00:13:29.909
and we're just using that
by setting the random seed

00:13:29.909 --> 00:13:33.145
using today's date.

00:13:33.145 --> 00:13:33.646
All right.

00:13:33.646 --> 00:13:35.614
So let's see here.

00:13:39.018 --> 00:13:39.518
OK.

00:13:39.518 --> 00:13:40.920
So now, we want to compare--

00:13:40.920 --> 00:13:43.022
we want to do some sort
of comparison to say,

00:13:43.022 --> 00:13:46.892
hey, is the word that
the person entered--

00:13:46.892 --> 00:13:50.229
if they make it past
this part there, like,

00:13:50.229 --> 00:13:53.532
how well does that match
up with the target word?

00:13:53.532 --> 00:13:55.467
And that's something
where it sort of-- it

00:13:55.467 --> 00:13:58.704
makes a lot of sense to put
that into its own function.

00:13:58.704 --> 00:14:02.875
And I will do that.

00:14:02.875 --> 00:14:06.412
Oh, I'll do that below
the server function.

00:14:06.412 --> 00:14:08.414
So let's say-- let's see.

00:14:08.414 --> 00:14:11.116
What should we call this?

00:14:11.116 --> 00:14:15.454
Check_word function
and then we'll

00:14:15.454 --> 00:14:24.763
say the target word and
the guess, all right?

00:14:24.763 --> 00:14:27.333
So we want to say check is--

00:14:27.333 --> 00:14:30.069
not just are these two words
the same, if it was that simple,

00:14:30.069 --> 00:14:31.871
we wouldn't need to
make a function for it,

00:14:31.871 --> 00:14:37.443
but in Wordle, we need
to know how many--

00:14:37.443 --> 00:14:40.379
which of these
letters in the guess

00:14:40.379 --> 00:14:43.816
is in the target word
